Great notes — adding a compact retry policy we use in our production clients (feel free to copy into the SDK examples):

1) Logical flow: on 429 or network error -> read Retry-After header; if present, sleep that long. Otherwise, exponential backoff with full jitter: sleep = random(0, base * 2^attempt) where base = 250ms.
2) Max attempts: 6 (to cover a slightly longer transient window for settlement spikes).
3) Circuit breaker: if we see >10% 500/502 errors over a 1-minute window, open CB and stop sending new requests for 30s, then probe.
4) Token rotation: confirm with Monica that ACME will post their new key to the portal prior to cutover; we will set a 15-minute overlap window where both keys are valid on our side for shadow testing.

Short sample (pseudo):
function sleep(ms) { return new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms)); }
async function attempt(req) {
  for (let i=0; i<6; i++) {
    try {
      const r = await http.post('/generate', req);
      if (r.status === 429) {
        const ra = Number(r.headers['retry-after'] || 0);
        if (ra > 0) { await sleep(ra*1000); continue; }
        const base = 250;
        const jitter = Math.floor(Math.random()*base*Math.pow(2,i));
        await sleep(jitter);
        continue;
      }
      return r;
    } catch (err) {
      // network error fallback
      await sleep(Math.floor(Math.random() * Math.min(8000, 250 * Math.pow(2,i))));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}

